THEOREM HE6.A assumes R_λ separable — Ore-regularity at the node. When an
ℓ ≥ 2 side carries a repeated factor, e.g. **R_λ = (Z−s)² with ℓ = 2,
L_λ = 4 = μ, D′ = 2, n = 8**, the outer read gives a single label class of
size D′L_λ = 8 = deg f and DOES NOT decide σ. HE3's §S6.3 treats this node
in one of two ways, and **neither is complete**:

* as a *stage-α refine*, "recentering the key at a K-rational residual root"
